{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb","id":1028179,"title":"Celerity and Climb","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-07T09:02:11-08:00","id":1028179,"title":"Celerity and Climb","content":"Heya. Yesterday during our game, a situation came up that had me quite stomped.<br /> <br /> My players were trying to avoid a flooding river and climbed up a very step hillside to do so. The difficulty was severe and I had calculated on them just failing and being swept away. However, one of the players suddenly said that he used celerity to appear on top of the the cliff and it had me rather stumped as I couldn't find any references to athletics or climb in the celerity description.<br /> <br /> In the end, we agreed on having the player multiply his successes for climbing rolls by 1+celerity dots (as he had 2, it multiplied his successed by 3). How would you handle celerity and climbing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:16:43-08:00","id":1028185,"title":"","content":"Celerity just makes you move fast in short bursts. You would still have to actually climb, and Celerity doesn't give you any ability to analyze your handhold and foothold options any faster than normal, which would make faster movement speed pretty useless when it comes to climbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:41:48-08:00","id":1028188,"title":"","content":"How doesn't it give you the ability to act faster? It makes you able to snatch weapons and such out of the hands of people and perform other amazing feats. I might be misreading it, but I can't find a clear reference to if your ability to analyze is increased or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T11:36:05-08:00","id":1028212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028188#post1028188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How doesn't it give you the ability to act faster? It makes you able to snatch weapons and such out of the hands of people and perform other amazing feats. I might be misreading it, but I can't find a clear reference to if your ability to analyze is increased or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It allows you to move faster, but not to process sensory information faster. The latter is what Quicken Sight is for (core book, page 145).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T11:37:14-08:00","id":1028214,"title":"","content":"Celerity would let the vampire climb faster, but would not actually help climb. So:<br /> <br /> If the problem is that it's slippery, and the vampire's ability to climb is being tested, roll an Athletics check, Celerity does not help.<br /> <br /> If the problem is that the water is rising fast, but the vampire's ability to climb is not being tested, then Celerity helps just as much as it does for walking or running.<br /> <br /> If both slipperiness and time are an issue, roll an Athletics check, and if the vampire succeeds, the action happens at Celerity's normal eyeblink speed. No test is necessary for the speed of the climb, any more than it would be for walking or running.<br /> <br /> As for whether vampires think faster, that's a bit nuanced, but the guideline is that it's a physical Discipline. A vampire can react and do physical things very fast, as if the reactions were honed through training. The vampire can't do complex logic, though, so it doesn't let her code or think up witty comebacks faster.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Charlaquin's also correct to cite Quickened Sight, which provides the bullet time reactions. A character with Quickened Sight processes sensory information and makes decisions based on it faster. She can also absorb information faster. It still doesn't speed up complex logic. So she can read a book faster, but to really <i>get</i> it and comment on it, she needs to react at normal speeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 01-07-2017, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T13:48:33-08:00","id":1028255,"title":"","content":"Wait... so you can't make vampire Johnny 5?<br /> <br /> If you could, any recommendation as to how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:08:21-08:00","id":1028263,"title":"","content":"A vampire robot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:23:26-08:00","id":1028268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028255#post1028255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... so you can't make vampire Johnny 5?<br /> <br /> If you could, any recommendation as to how?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quicken Sight should do it. Basically, Celerity would allow you to flip through the encyclopedia and look at all the words in a few short moments, but not to process the &quot;Input!!!&quot;. Adding Auspex in the form of a Devotion will allow you to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:27:21-08:00","id":1028269,"title":"","content":"Maybe it is a case of mistaken identity but isn't Auspex already a part of the Quicken Sight devotion? :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:27:59-08:00","id":1028270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028263#post1028263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire robot?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would just be the case of embracing me. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:54:34-08:00","id":1028286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028269#post1028269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it is a case of mistaken identity but isn't Auspex already a part of the Quicken Sight devotion? :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wait, I misread Rose's post. I thought she was saying Celerity let you read a book fast but Quicken Sight was needed to &quot;get&quot; it. Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T15:12:44-08:00","id":1028291,"title":"","content":"Huh. Well, it doesn't particularly make or break a game, nor does it bother me. I just like all my potentials to remain intact, if possible. :P<br /> <br /> Homebrew idea: Reading with Quickened Sight gives you the 'skim' version and is therefore ripe for armchair speculation. You still need to think about the text, and even revisit it for deep meaning, but you are otherwise equipped to unpack it. That way, you can blitz the newspaper while Kant remains a challenge. Equally, forcing your way into an academic discipline; no. Keeping up with the scientific Jones by relying upon your previous framework; yes. Sound Fair?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T15:37:40-08:00","id":1028294,"title":"","content":"I'd say Celerity certainly WOULD help climb up a muddy slope as you can paw at the mud faster to find or dig out hand/footholds. Even without handholds, has anyone every riddin a quad through mud with paddles tires? They just slap the mud and push it out behind you which converts that energy into forward motion for the quad.<br /> <br /> Now a sheer rock face may be different but even then, when you scramble to get up something, it sometimes works better than going slowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 01-07-2017, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T17:20:37-08:00","id":1028340,"title":"","content":"I would say if you need a fast-info power, it's more Auspex than Celerity. Single-Discipline Devotion, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T02:39:53-08:00","id":1028471,"title":"","content":"The player in question did have Quicken sight, but I'm not sure I buy the answer that you need quicken sight. How does the vampire use celerity in the first place and why does it add to your defense if it doesn't increase reflexes and increase the speed at which the vampire can process what he sees? I've always interpreted Quicken Sight as the ability to use celerity without moving. A more limited usage of celerity that also makes you faster in that specific instance than what you would be with your regular celerity. A vampire with celerity 2 would perhaps act as celerity 4 for his quicken sight, for whatever purposes that would be necessary to know.<br /> <br /> Regardless of that, how would you handle the situation with Quicken Sight and Celerity both turned on then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:08:31-08:00","id":1028553,"title":"","content":"I think that if you have Eidetic Memory you can read super fast then sit down and meditate on it.<br /> <br /> Useful if you only have little time with a document or something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:37:50-08:00","id":1028586,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028471#post1028471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Regardless of that, how would you handle the situation with Quicken Sight and Celerity both turned on then?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">My reading would be:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">When you activate Quicken Sight, you activate its parts. It is not a separate discipline, just a novel expression of pre-existing disciplines. Activating Celerity and Quicken Sight is basically activating Celerity and Auspex together. In the situation where you don't manifest Celerity's speed boast or other boons, it might appear as if you are using enhanced Auspex alone but Celerity is 'on'. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">So I'd handle it by saying that Celerity doesn't allow you to 'soak' the information you receive without Auspex. You aren't seeing bullets and avoiding them as an act of will. You are bringing forth the Beast and through a combination of Beastly reaction and just being hard to hit, your body avoids damage while the Man is along for the ride. To the Man, moving in Celerity is as strange as walking; it is something he does without any thought. Auspex (via Quicken Sight) adds the thought element. This leads into the discussion of Eidetic Memory...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028214#post1028214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She can also absorb information faster. It still doesn't speed up complex logic. So she can read a book faster, but to really get it and comment on it, she needs to react at normal speeds.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1028179-celerity-and-climb?p=1028553#post1028553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that if you have Eidetic Memory you can read super fast then sit down and meditate on it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">First off, excellent idea bringing Eidetic Memory into this. It gives those who bought it a suitable 'hack' and I just love it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The idea of 'read then ruminate' was what I was going for in my previous post. The idea is that, building off of what Rose said, Auspex gives you access to the 'thoughts' the Beast runs through while acting under Celerity. Basically, the Man makes a copy of all that useless info the Beast would otherwise scrap. Under my original reading, that was sufficient to have all the information. However, as it is just recording but not processing, I'm now of the opinion one needs to not only successfully remember what they read (and a whole book is something the mind would rather off-load) but you then need to think about it. For those with Eidetic Memory, the first step is auto-completed. They are use to remembering detail, so they only have to process it now. Whereas others have to get the idea right, then think about the idea. If they read something easy or familiar or just want the barebones, then the task is easy. If they try to blitz Hegel, they may just forget everything because Hegel is someone you process first in order to remember (unless you just brute-remember, which is the case with Eidetic Memory and why this step is auto-completed). So Johnny 5 is still possible, but now a little more unique as other traits are required in conjunction with the discipline requirement.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Returning to the original topic then, we can reconcile the need to process information with the inaccessibility of that information. If it is climbable under normal conditions, speed and reaction help. If it is not climbable, speed grants no boon. (Other than the sort suggested by Rathamus, which I would leave to ST-discretion as, depending on group knowledge, it may or may not be accepted as 'plausible'. I don't deny Rathamus' claims, just suggest that sometimes <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RealityIsUnrealistic\" target=\"_blank\">Reality is Unrealistic.</a>) If you activate Quicken Sight, all you add is the capacity to note where the Beast planted their foot or what they grabbed. It wouldn't assist you at all in my opinion.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Lastly, to cap this off and after re-reading the Quicken Sight merit, the intent was never to give me vampire Johnny 5. Heck, you can even fail to succeed with this devotion, which would make speed reading unreliable if the check was page based. Don't know why I read it into that power but it isn't in the text. So, sorry about the derailment I guess. -_-</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}